# YES/NO questions (2026-11-15). A station asks, the pilot answers with the radio's YES or NO key (no answer is NO), and the asker replies.
# The ask events open the prompt only when their line goes on air; the yes/no events are the replies.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- command: contracts

@command.askcontract tactical
[*] New tasking on the board: <title>. Can you take it?
[*] Command has work for you. <title>. Will you take it?
[*] Contract up: <title>. You want it?
[*] We need a flight on <title>. Are you available?
[*] Priority job: <title>. Can you handle it?
[* night] Night work, if you want it: <title>. Taking it?

@command.contractyes status
[*] Copy. It is yours. Marked on your HUD.
[*] Good. Contract is assigned to you. Do not let us down.
[*] Acknowledged. You have the job. Target data is on your display.
[*] Copy that. Tasking confirmed. Good hunting.
[*] Understood. It is on your board now.

@command.contractno status
[*] Understood. We will pass it on.
[*] Copy. Another flight will take it.
[*] Negative, copied. It stays on the board.
[*] Roger. We will find someone else.

@command.contractdone status
[*] Contract complete: <title>. Payment is on its way.
[*] Good work. <title> is done. The money is wired.
[*] Command confirms <title> complete. Nicely done.
[*] That is the job done. Funds transferred.
[*] Tasking complete. Command is pleased.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- command: OPS perks

@command.askperk tactical
[*] OPS here. <perk> is ready. Want it?
[*] <perk> is up and waiting on your word. Use it?
[*] OPS has <perk> on standby. Do you want it?
[*] <perk> is ready for tasking. Shall we arm it?

@command.perkyes status
[*] Armed. Put your aim on the target.
[*] Copy, it is armed. Aim where you want it.
[*] Armed and waiting. Point it and call it.

@command.perkno status
[*] Understood. Holding it in reserve.
[*] Copy. It stays on the shelf.
[*] Roger. We keep it ready.

@command.askfire tactical
[*] <perk> is armed on your aim. Fire?
[*] Your aim is the target. Release <perk>?
[*] Standing by on <perk>. Send it?

@command.fireyes status
[*] Fired. Stand by for effect.
[*] Release confirmed. It is on its way.
[*] Shot away. Watch the target.

@command.fireno status
[*] Holding. It stays armed until you call it.
[*] Copy, holding fire.
[*] Understood. Standing by.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- command: VANGUARD drones

@command.askdrones tactical
[*] Vanguard here. Drones are up and you have a target. Send them?
[*] Your drones can take that target. Commit them?
[*] Drones on station. Want them on your target?
[*] Vanguard control. Shall we put the drones on it?

@command.dronesyes status
[*] Drones committed. Moving to your target.
[*] Copy. Drones are on it.
[*] Vanguard is engaging your target.

@command.dronesno status
[*] Understood. Drones hold.
[*] Copy, drones stay on task.
[*] Roger, drones holding.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- wing: engage and clear the six (text only: the wingmen are not recorded)

@wingask.engage tactical
[*] <lead>, that bandit is in reach. Permission to engage?
[*] Request permission to engage, <lead>.
[*] Bandit in range. Do we engage?
[*] Clear us in, <lead>? Say the word.

@wingask.engageyes tactical
[*] Copy! Engaging!
[*] Cleared hot. We are going in.
[*] Roger, committing on the bandit.

@wingask.engageno status
[*] Copy, holding formation.
[*] Understood. Staying on your wing.
[*] Roger, we hold.

@wingask.six emergency
[*] <lead>, you have a shooter on you! Want me on your six?
[*] Missile on you, <lead>! I can clear your six. Say it!
[*] You are spiked! Want me to cover you?

@wingask.sixyes tactical
[*] On my way! Hang in there!
[*] Moving to your six. Keep turning!
[*] I have you covered. Coming in!

@wingask.sixno status
[*] Copy, staying on task.
[*] Understood. Good luck.
[*] Roger. Holding position.
